  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I reviewed all 7 patients on the 10/19 DOAC list under RBC-PHARM-07. Five doses ended up changed and two stayed the same. Four results or documents came in while I worked and changed decisions on four patients. Each change has a signed progress note with the values and records cited.\n\n1. Castellano (pt-0061): apixaban increased from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She meets none of the dose criteria (age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02), and the ID letter of 9/10 says her itraconazole course ended 8/14.\n2. Delgado (pt-0003): rivaroxaban stays at 20 mg daily (mr-t0011). I first lowered it to 15 mg based on St. Brigid's creatinine of 160 µmol/L (CrCl 44 mL/min). St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault, giving CrCl 59.9 mL/min, so I reversed the change and recorded why.\n3. Duquette (pt-0041): apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005). He meets no dose criteria, but he has an active itraconazole order (mr-00359). I didn't change the itraconazole.\n4. Fairweather (pt-0062): apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0012). His clinic labs supported 5 mg, but a St. Brigid ED creatinine from 10/21 arrived during the review: 150 µmol/L (1.70 mg/dL). With age 82, that makes two criteria.\n5. Moravec (pt-0038): rivaroxaban increased from 15 to 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). The May reduction used ideal body weight; on his actual 96 kg, CrCl is 56.1 mL/min. He later sent a portal message with a home-scale weight of 185 lb. That isn't a measured weight under the policy, so the dose stands, and I added a chart note saying so.\n6. Pellegrino (pt-0043): rivaroxaban lowered from 20 to 15 mg daily (mr-t0013). The 10/7 labs supported 20 mg, but a new creatinine of 1.25 on 10/22 gives CrCl 43.6 mL/min.\n7. Vance (pt-0002): apixaban ends at 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0014). I first raised it to 5 mg because he's back to 64.9 kg with SCr 1.21, leaving age as his only criterion. Then a St. Brigid dermatology letter arrived saying he started itraconazole on 10/22, so I put it back to 2.5 mg and recorded why.\n\nNo other medications were changed. I closed the five inbox items that arrived during the review; your other open inbox items aren't part of this list, and I left them alone. No other new items had come in when I finished.\n\nFollow-up worth considering (no tasks created):\n- **Duquette and Vance:** review apixaban again when their itraconazole courses end (Vance's around mid-January 2027).\n- **Fairweather:** repeat creatinine after the ED visit.\n- **Moravec:** get a measured clinic weight. If it confirms about 84 kg, his CrCl would be about 49 mL/min and the dose would need review.\n- **Rivaroxaban sigs:** the reissued orders may not carry \"with the evening meal\". The notes state it; it's worth checking the pharmacy instructions.",
